7. Ng5 { Hits f7 with the knight and the bishop on b3, as in the Fried Liver of the Italian. Riskier than 7.c3, because Black has a good answer. [%cal Gg5f7,Gb3f7] } 7... d5 { The right defence: it blocks the bishop. } 8. exd5 Nd4 { The best reply: Black gives a pawn but hits the bishop on b3. } ( 8... Nxd5 $2 9. Nxf7 { The knight takes the pawn only the king guards, and attacks the queen and the rook. } 9... Kxf7 10. Qf3+ { Check, and the queen attacks the knight on d5, which the bishop pins to the king. [%cal Gf3d5,Gb3d5] } 10... Ke6 ( 10... Ke8 11. Bxd5 { Wins the knight back and hits the knight on c6. } 11... Nd4 12. Qf7# { Mate, as in Scholar's mate: the bishop on d5 guards the queen. } ) 11. Nc3 { Piles up on the pinned knight. Black's king is stuck in the middle and the engine gives White a winning attack. } ) 9. d3 { Opens the bishop on c1 and keeps c4 and e4 covered. The game is level. } 9... Bc5 10. Be3 { Meets the bishop on c5 and covers f2. } *
